 - [ ] **PREVIEW-003**: When concurrent requests miss the cache for the same preview key, the system SHALL return 202 with the same job ticket and a two-second retry interval while one shared render job is pending.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict entries before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-005**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-006**: When a preview is admitted to the cache for the first time, the system SHALL place it at the head of the Am queue (first-use queue).
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-007**: When a cached preview in the Am queue is accessed a second time, the system SHALL promote it to the head of the A1 queue (reuse queue).
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-008**: When a cached preview in the A1 queue is accessed, the system SHALL move it to the head of the A1 queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-009**: When the Am queue would exceed its budget (25% of 12 GiB), the system SHALL evict entries from the tail of Am before admission.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-010**: When the A1 queue would exceed its budget (75% of 12 GiB) and Am has no evictable entries, the system SHALL evict entries from the tail of A1 before admission.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-011**: When an entry is evicted from the A1 queue, the system SHALL admit it to the head of the Am queue if space permits.
